## Context
Parent: 1229. `yawn` is project-oriented and currently has no check comparing
a project's own directives against the harness.

Scope: project `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/`,
`.claude/skills/`, `.agents/skills/` against the loaded harness rules and
skills. Never the harness against itself (that is 1233). In the harness repo
itself the check is a `skip`.

Findings, three kinds, each with a *why*:
- contradiction: a local instruction that inverts a harness instruction;
- shadowing: a local skill or rule with a harness name (mechanical), or one
  taking a harness skill's responsibility (judged);
- repeated procedure: a local copy of a harness procedure.

A local override that states its reason in place is `ok (reasoned)`; a
silent override or a copy is `warn`. Example of reasoned: arena's
`CLAUDE.md` replaces merge-by-PR with `git merge --no-ff` because the repo
has no forge.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Name-collision shadowing is a script under `scripts/`, called from the
      yawn body, with a test that fires on a fixture project shadowing a
      harness skill name (positive control) and stays quiet on one that does not
- [ ] Judged findings read skill descriptions first and full bodies only where
      descriptions overlap
- [ ] Each finding names the local file, the harness file, and the
      governing instruction; output fits the existing yawn report format
- [ ] Degrades to `skip` with a reason when the project has no local directives
- [ ] `yawn` stays a reporter: no fixes, no tickets

## Imagine (raid 2026-10-27)

**Premise holds.** `skills/yawn/SKILL.md:33-104` (checks 1-13) has no local-versus-harness comparison; the only pass is the prompt at `scripts/prompt-project-coherence.sh:40`, called from `scripts/on-start-context.sh:36-38`, whose lines 17-31 enumerate exactly this ticket's local sources.

**Simplest path.** (1) `scripts/project_shadow.py <project>`: local skill and rule names against harness `skills/*` and `rules/*`, reusing `skill_frontmatter.load` (`scripts/skill_frontmatter.py:44`); JSON, one line per collision (local file, harness file, governing instruction). (2) Move the harness-self and linked-worktree guard (`prompt-project-coherence.sh:9-14`) into the script so the harness yields `skip`; 1232 deletes the prompt script and would otherwise lose it. (3) Yawn check 14: run the script, then the judged pass (descriptions first, bodies only on overlap); one table row plus bullets, placed before Output format. (4) `tests/test_project_shadow.py` with tmp fixture projects (positive: shadows a harness skill name; negative: does not).

**Antipatterns.** YAGNI: no Python prose parsing for contradictions; the judged part stays with the model. Duplication: share the source enumeration or note two small lists.

**Criterion proposals.** (a) The script emits the `skip` reason; test the harness-self and the no-directives skips. (b) `ok (reasoned)` made operational: the reason sits in the same file within a few lines of the override; arena `CLAUDE.md` "no remote" is the live fixture. (c) Output is stable for 1231, which routes it.

**Blind-spot pass (raid 2026-10-27), folded in.** (1) Scope includes the project's own top-level `skills/*` when they are projected into the user skill namespace (arena's `skills/arena`, linked from `~/.claude/skills/arena`), not only `.claude/skills/` and `.agents/skills/`. (2) Project skill roots are per runtime (Vibe `.vibe/skills`, `adapters/pilot-support.json:55`; Pi, Codex): take the folder list from the adapter declarations, not a hardcoded list, and judge shadowing against each runtime's precedence. (3) yawn is the cross-runtime proof slice (`adapters/README.md:142-152`): the check calls its script through the runtime-supplied `IDH_ROOT` seam and `tests/test_skill_seam.py` passes. (4) The finding record is the 1231 contract: kind, local file, harness file, governing instruction, verdict (`ok (reasoned)` / `warn`), proposed disposition and destination (project or harness); `tests/test_yawn_molt_suggestion.py` pins the shared yawn/molt text. Raid assumption, author may overrule: the judged half also runs when molt calls yawn from lair, since it is scoped to one project with local directives.

## Plan (raid 2026-10-27)
Actions:
1. `scripts/project_shadow.py <project>`: JSON on stdout. Skip record
   `{"status":"skip","reason":...}` for the harness or a linked worktree of it
   (port the git-common-dir test of `prompt-project-coherence.sh:9-14`) and for no
   local directive source.
2. Collisions: harness names = `skills/*/SKILL.md` (via `skill_frontmatter.load`) and
   `rules/*.md` stems; local = dirs with a SKILL.md under each project skill root,
   `.claude/rules/*.md`, and top-level `skills/*` (arena). One record per collision
   with the 1231 fields: kind, local_file, harness_file, instruction (harness
   description), verdict, disposition, destination. Malformed local SKILL.md gives a
   record with a reason, never a crash.
3. Skill roots are data: add `project_skill_roots` per harness in
   `adapters/pilot-support.json` (claude `.claude/skills`; codex/pi `.agents/skills`;
   vibe `.vibe/skills` + `.agents/skills`); the script reads it.
4. `ok (reasoned)`: reason marker (`because`, `since`, `has no`) within 5 lines of the
   override in the same file; else `warn`. Name collisions only; contradiction and
   repeats stay judged.
5. `skills/yawn/SKILL.md`: check 14 (script through the existing `$IDH_ROOT` seam,
   then judged pass: descriptions first, bodies only on overlap), one table row, bullets
   with local file, harness file, instruction. Reporter only; `ok (reasoned)` never
   enters the Action plan; contract headings untouched.
6. One sentence in `adapters/README.md` yawn paragraph.
First failing test, `tests/test_project_shadow.py::test_name_collision_is_found`:
tmp non-git project (GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES) with `.claude/skills/yawn/SKILL.md` and
`.claude/skills/mine/SKILL.md`, run against the real harness. Assert exactly one
record: kind shadowing, local_file ends `.claude/skills/yawn/SKILL.md`, harness_file
ends `skills/yawn/SKILL.md`, verdict warn, no `mine`. Negative twin: only `mine`, zero
records.
Others: harness/worktree skip; no-directives skip; `.vibe/skills/yawn` and top-level
`skills/yawn` found; reasoned vs unreasoned CLAUDE.md gives `ok (reasoned)` vs `warn`;
extend `test_yawn_molt_suggestion`. Antipatterns: the `mine` and exact-one asserts defeat a
"flag everything" version; the reasoned pair differs only by reason text; the vibe root is
absent from code defaults, so not tautological. Dependencies: none upstream; feeds 1231 (record contract) and 1232 (guard moved here
before the prompt script is deleted).
PLAN WARN: criterion 2 and the contradiction/repeat kinds are model judgment in skill
text; only skill-text assertions are testable.
Files: scripts/project_shadow.py, tests/test_project_shadow.py, skills/yawn/SKILL.md,
tests/test_yawn_molt_suggestion.py, adapters/pilot-support.json, adapters/README.md
(check no schema test rejects the new field).

## Feasibility (raid 2026-10-27): WARN
- Canonical finding record (shared with 1231), JSON lines, one object per line: `kind` (shadowing|contradiction|repeat), `local_file`, `harness_file`, `instruction`, `verdict` (`ok`|`warn`; "ok (reasoned)" is yawn display text only), `reason` (str|null), `disposition` (delete-local|annotate|harness-ticket|null), `destination` (project|harness). Skip is one line `{"status":"skip","reason":...}`. The script leaves `disposition` null on warn (redundant vs deliberate is not mechanical); yawn's judged pass fills it.
- Plan step 4 says reason detection is for name collisions only, but the listed test "reasoned vs unreasoned CLAUDE.md" is a contradiction (judged) case. Fix: scan for the reason marker in the colliding local SKILL.md/rule file; drop the CLAUDE.md pair from the script tests (arena's merge override is judged-path evidence, checked at the 1229 integration review).
- Pi's project root is `.pi/skills/` as well as `.agents/skills/` (shipped `docs/skills.md:35,61`); add it to pi's `project_skill_roots`. `adapters/perch.py` and the tests that read pilot-support.json do no key whitelist, so the new field is safe.
- 1232 calls `project_shadow.py --is-harness PROJECT`, which this plan does not define. Either add it (exit 0 harness or linked worktree, 1 otherwise, stdlib only, decided before importing yaml), or let 1232 inline the shell guard (recommended there).
- `skill_frontmatter.load` is at line 35, not 44. It raises `FrontmatterError`: catch that for the malformed-SKILL.md record.
- yawn check 13 sits after `## Action plan` (SKILL.md:174), not inside 1-12. Put check 14 after 13, and add table rows to Output format. Keep `**skip**` from appearing on a line of its own in the new text, or `test_contract_headings_untouched` breaks.
- Do not edit `tests/test_yawn_molt_suggestion.py`: its one test already pins the headings. 1231 owns the single molt-wiring assertion there, which avoids a W1/W2 edit on the same lines.
- The check-14 command must read `python3 "$IDH_ROOT/scripts/project_shadow.py"`. A bare `scripts/x.py` in skills/ trips `make check-agnostic-skills`. No keys or network needed.
